  "name": "Wavre",
  "date": "18–19 June 1815",
  "campaign": "hundred-days",
  "summary": "Sent after the Prussians with a third of the army, Grouchy caught Thielemann's corps holding the crossings of the Dyle at Wavre while the rest of Blücher's army marched to Waterloo. The French fought for the bridges into the night and won the field the next morning, too late and too far away to matter.",
